Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-23
Subject: Store ncnv printnodeinfo's convtyp2str as string[255] instead of pchar
License: expat

`ttypeconvnode.printnodeinfo` keeps a per-`tconverttype` name table:

  convtyp2str : array[tconverttype] of pchar = (
    'tc_none', 'tc_equal', 'tc_not_possible', ...);
  ...
  write(t, ', convtype = ', strpas(convtyp2str[convtype]));

The typed-const initializer relies on Pascal's "string-literal decays
to pchar" rule for typed constants -- each entry is the address of the
string literal in the binary's read-only data. The read site then
calls `strpas` to convert each pchar back to a Pascal string for
`write`.

tp2cc does not lower typed-const arrays of `pchar` initialized from
string literals into a clean C++ form (the literals would have to land
in a separate storage area whose addresses are then captured into the
array initializer; const-expression initialization across translation
units gets tangled). Storing the entries as `string[255]` puts the
shortstring data inline in the array, no pchar storage needed and no
`strpas` at the read site.

--- a/compiler/ncnv.pas
+++ b/compiler/ncnv.pas
@@ -606,7 +622,7 @@

     procedure ttypeconvnode.printnodeinfo(var t : text);
       const
-        convtyp2str : array[tconverttype] of pchar = (
+        convtyp2str : array[tconverttype] of string[255] = (
           'tc_none',
           'tc_equal',
           'tc_not_possible',
@@ -650,7 +666,7 @@
         );
       begin
         inherited printnodeinfo(t);
-        write(t,', convtype = ',strpas(convtyp2str[convtype]));
+        write(t,', convtype = ',convtyp2str[convtype]);
       end;


